---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE_NAME, AUTHOR_EMAIL, APP_VERSION } from "../consts";
const updated = "July 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How MindScope handles your data: what the accessibility services access, what is sent for AI analysis, and how it's stored."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <section class="hero-gradient">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16 text-center">
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">
        Privacy Policy
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-white/80">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-14">
    <div
      class="mb-10 rounded-2xl border border-sky/20 bg-sky-pale/20 p-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-navy-soft"
    >
      <strong class="text-navy">In plain terms:</strong> MindScope needs powerful
      Android permissions to do its job. It reads on-screen content to detect blocked
      sections and to check chats for harmful language. This page explains exactly what
      it accesses, what leaves your device, and why.
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-navy-soft">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy">1. What MindScope accesses</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-navy">On-screen section detection.</strong> The
            Accessibility Service reads the currently visible screen only to
            recognise which section of a supported app (Instagram, YouTube,
            WhatsApp) is open, so it can show the blocking overlay.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-navy">Chat text.</strong> When chat analysis is
            enabled, message text from monitored conversations is captured so it
            can be scored for harmful/toxic language.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-navy">App usage timing.</strong> For screen-time
            control, the app tracks how long selected apps are used to enforce
            your limits.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-navy">Account details.</strong> Your email and a
            securely hashed password are used to create and access your account.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy">2. What leaves your device</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Section detection and screen-time enforcement run <strong class="text-navy"
            >entirely on your device</strong
          >. For chat analysis, captured message text is sent over an encrypted
          connection to MindScope's backend and to Google's Gemini AI to compute a
          toxicity score and feedback. The resulting scores and your analytics are
          stored against your account so you can view trends over time.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy">3. Third-party processing</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Chat and voice content submitted for analysis is processed by Google's
          Gemini API. That processing is subject to Google's applicable terms and
          privacy practices. MindScope does not sell your data or use it for
          advertising.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy">4. Data storage &amp; security</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          <li>Passwords are hashed (bcrypt); the app never stores them in plain text.</li>
          <li>Authentication uses signed tokens (JWT) kept in secure device storage.</li>
          <li>Analysis results and analytics are stored in the app's backend database.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy">5. Permissions you grant</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          MindScope asks for Accessibility Service access and, on some devices,
          autostart / battery / pop-up permissions so it can run reliably in the
          background. You can revoke any of these at any time in your Android
          settings — some features will stop working until they're re-enabled.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy">6. Your control</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Every feature is opt-in and individually toggleable. Turn off chat
          analysis and no message text is captured or sent. Uninstalling the app
          removes its on-device data.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-navy">7. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Questions about privacy? Email
          <a href={`mailto:${AUTHOR_EMAIL}`} class="font-semibold text-sky hover:underline">
            {AUTHOR_EMAIL}
          </a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="border-t border-slate-200 pt-6 text-xs text-muted">
        This policy applies to {SITE_NAME} for Android (v{APP_VERSION}). It may be
        updated as the app evolves; material changes will be reflected on this page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
